@auth.sigil from Auth import { identity and access, renter }
@resource-management.sigil from ResourceManagement import {
    Room,
    base availability rules,
    requested time range,
    room availability answer,
}
@scheduling-and-recurrence.sigil from SchedulingAndRecurrence import {
    recurring booking series,
}

component Booking {
    goal {
        Creates and manages a *booking request* and *confirmed booking* while
        preserving base availability rules, recurrence, and access boundaries.
    }

    interface {
        A renter starts a booking request for a Room and a requested time range.

        Before confirmation, Booking sends the Room and full requested time range to
        Resource Management for a room availability answer based on
        base availability rules.

        Booking requires a recurring booking series to confirm each occurrence of a
        repeated booking request.

        A confirmed booking records its Room, renter, requested time range, and
        confirmation status.

        A renter can cancel a confirmed booking that they own; Booking records a
        *cancellation record* subject to the cancellation rules.
    }

    state {
        Booking owns booking request, confirmed booking, and cancellation record.

        Booking exclusively owns the recurring booking series.

        A booking request can be pending, confirmed, rejected, or canceled.
    }

    logic {
        Booking checks a renter's permission through identity and access and asks
        Resource Management for a full-range room availability answer for the Room.

        If identity and access denies permission for a booking request, Booking
        rejects it and returns a rejection result that ends that path.

        If the room availability answer denies the full range or a *booking conflict*
        exists with a confirmed booking, Booking rejects the request and ends that
        path.

        For a single-time booking request, Booking confirms only when permission,
        availability, and conflict checks pass, then returns the confirmed booking
        and ends that path.

        For a repeated booking request, Booking uses the recurring booking series
        to identify each occurrence. It confirms only when permission, availability,
        and conflict checks pass for every occurrence, then returns the confirmed
        booking and ends that path.

        When a renter cancels a confirmed booking, Booking creates a cancellation
        record, preserves booking history, returns the canceled booking, and ends that
        path.
    }

    constraints {
        Booking must not require a recurring booking series to confirm each repeated
        booking request.

        Booking owns booking conflict checks and does not read Resource Management's
        private Room data or availability logic.

        identity and access supplies current-user and permission checks. Booking
        does not own users, sessions, roles, or permission policy.

        Scheduling and Recurrence owns the recurring booking series; Booking uses
        its public contract for repeated requests.
    }

    cases {
        A renter requests a Room for a range that fits its base availability rules
        and has no booking conflict; Booking confirms when identity and access permits.

        A renter requests a range that overlaps an existing confirmed booking;
        Booking rejects the request due to the booking conflict.

        A renter cancels a confirmed booking; Booking retains its cancellation record
        and booking history.
    }
}
